WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:01.601
We focus

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.402
the election on the

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:04.671
past or on other side issues.

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:06.339
Then I think the Democrats

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.742
are going to beat us again.

00:00:09.109 --> 00:00:10.410
Welcome back to State of the Union.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:11.277
That was Florida Governor

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:13.113
Ron DeSantis in Iowa yesterday

00:00:13.113 --> 00:00:14.280
making his pitch

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.017
to 20, 24 Republican primary voters.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.218
My panel joins me now.

00:00:18.218 --> 00:00:21.388
Nice to see everybody Scott Jennings,

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:24.290
he not only was out in Iowa,

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:25.892
he also Ron

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:29.262
DeSantis seems to be reacting to

00:00:29.262 --> 00:00:33.700
and changing a bit as it as it goes

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.136
with his critics

00:00:36.136 --> 00:00:38.371
saying he's not engaging enough, he's

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.572
not glad-handing

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.841
he's not looking people in the eye

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.843
the way that Iowa voters,

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.412
New Hampshire voters

00:00:45.412 --> 00:00:48.281
have an expectation of their candidates.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:49.249
Yeah.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:50.283
And he did a great job

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:50.550
with it

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.418
yesterday in Iowa,

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:51.751
rolled out

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.820
a bunch of endorsements, had a good day.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.321
Donald Trump canceled his event.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:55.922
Some people say

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:57.490
it was because of the weather.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.359
Other people say it was because he

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:00.627
wasn't able to draw a big crowd.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:01.861
I don't know what the truth is,

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:02.796
but there's some evidence

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:03.897
for that theory.

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:06.032
I thought DeSantis had a nice right.

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:06.399
By the way, he's

00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:07.534
not even a candidate yet.

00:01:07.534 --> 00:01:09.002
But to me, the most important thing

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:09.836
he did

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.071
was make an argument about

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:13.540
what is the purpose of a political party?

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.542
The purpose of a party is to beat

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:16.676
the Democrats.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:18.711
The Republican Party, in this case,

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.180
and we don't Trump

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.047
doesn't have a plan to beat

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:21.648
the Democrats.

00:01:21.648 --> 00:01:22.649
He has a plan to dominate

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:23.450
the Republican Party.

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:24.684
DeSantis wants the party

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.820
to be an electoral function,

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:27.887
and Trump wants the party

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.255
to be a bludgeoning tool

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.558
against the people that Republicans hate,

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:34.494
whether that CNN or the media or whoever

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:36.096
one of their institutions,

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.697
DeSantis wants it to win elections

00:01:37.697 --> 00:01:39.265
and I thought that was the best message

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:40.066
he could have had yesterday.

00:01:40.066 --> 00:01:41.601
Listen, I think Trump world would have

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:43.236
had you believe that the town hall

00:01:43.236 --> 00:01:44.637
this past week was a huge victory

00:01:44.637 --> 00:01:45.572
and a win for them.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.040
But I think the reality is a lot of

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.508
Republican observers were watching

00:01:48.508 --> 00:01:49.309
and saying that man didn't

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:50.877
win a single additional vote.

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:52.912
And I think it emboldened challengers

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:53.480
like Iran.

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:54.147
DeSantis, who,

00:01:54.147 --> 00:01:56.182
of course, isn't announced yet

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.817
to go out and make a different case.

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:58.318
Remind them,

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:59.319
you don't want the drama,

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.520
you don't want the noise,

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.654
you don't want your blood pressure

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:02.388
growing up.

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:03.756
It was a good day for him.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.325
My one critique of DeSantis

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:06.693
at this juncture would be

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.528
you have two jobs in a primary, raise

00:02:08.528 --> 00:02:09.496
your name ID

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:10.897
and take out the competition.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:11.664
And there is someone

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:12.999
who's polling in double digits

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:13.800
ahead of him,

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.268
and he's not directly going

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.336
after Trump enough.

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:16.903
His PAC

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:17.670
is, to be honest,

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.538
the Never Back Down

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:19.439
PAC is a really good

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:20.940
candidate itself right now.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.475
But DeSantis has kind of waffled

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:24.210
on actually challenging Trump,

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.278
which is something he's going to.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:25.712
I wonder

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.180
I wonder if he will change that

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.548
when he actually does run.

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:29.449
I want to get to

00:02:29.449 --> 00:02:30.049
but I want to

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.618
first you mentioned

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.286
the CNN town hall

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.555
and the fact that part of the strategy

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:37.390
there was to get Donald Trump

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.626
to expand beyond his base.

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.761
The content of what he said

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:44.364
might have posed some challenges.

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:45.698
Let's listen to some of that.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.602
Will you pardon the January six

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:52.172
rioters who were convicted

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.940
of federal offenses?

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.609
I am inclined to pardon many of them.

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:59.145
Getting rid of Roe v Wade

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:00.880
was an incredible thing

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.448
and I was very honored to do it.

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:05.418
Do you want Ukraine to win this war?

00:03:05.418 --> 00:03:06.252
I don't think in

00:03:06.252 --> 00:03:07.587
terms of winning and losing.

00:03:07.587 --> 00:03:09.255
I think in terms of getting it settled.

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:12.992
So we stop killing all these people.

00:03:13.326 --> 00:03:14.427
Michael LaRosa, first of all,

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:17.096
welcome to the State of the Union panel.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.632
You worked for the Bidens for

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:20.099
for a while.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:21.434
You worked in the Biden administration.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:22.502
What's your view

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:25.104
of how Democrats can or will use

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.506
comments like this?

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:26.673
Well,

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:27.740
I think you just provided

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:28.675
a lot of material,

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.410
but that material was already there

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:30.877
anyway.

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:31.978
I don't think he

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.413
I don't think he added much.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:35.014
I think you saw a preview,

00:03:35.014 --> 00:03:35.848
thanks to CNN,

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.917
a preview to what the

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:39.552
next campaign is going to look like

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:40.920
from the

00:03:40.920 --> 00:03:41.788
candidates, but also

00:03:41.788 --> 00:03:43.923
from from the audience at home.

00:03:43.957 --> 00:03:44.991
This is what we're going to be watching

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:47.760
for the next year and a half again.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.963
I think that when it comes to Trump,

00:03:49.963 --> 00:03:51.297
I look, of course,

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:52.165
the Biden campaign

00:03:52.165 --> 00:03:53.633
would love to run against Donald Trump

00:03:53.633 --> 00:03:54.334
because we know

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.736
we know there's hard data on Trump.

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:57.203
Right.

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:58.404
We know that independents

00:03:58.404 --> 00:03:59.839
have now run away from him

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.975
three times three elections in a row.

00:04:02.108 --> 00:04:03.543
And that's something that you feel safe

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:03.876
with.

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.645
You know what you're running against

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:06.679
with anybody else.

00:04:06.679 --> 00:04:08.114
That's it's

00:04:08.114 --> 00:04:09.115
it's going to be a challenge

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:10.817
for President Biden

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:12.719
because nothing you fear more in

00:04:12.719 --> 00:04:14.520
politics is an X factor.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.588
We don't know how

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:16.055
how Ron

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.658
DeSantis tests across the country.

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:20.827
Well, I mean, I think

00:04:20.827 --> 00:04:22.662
right now there's Republican infighting,

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:23.896
which I'm fine with.

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.466
But I will say that.

00:04:26.799 --> 00:04:27.166
Okay.

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.901
Nobody wants to go back to the past

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.536
of relitigating the 2020 election

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:31.838
Donald Trump laws.

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.640
But when you hear Ron DeSantis in Iowa

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.642
saying what country do we want for it?

00:04:35.642 --> 00:04:36.476
A lot of Americans

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:37.343
don't want the country

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:38.611
that Ron DeSantis is painting

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:39.912
either with culture wars

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:41.581
with a six week abortion ban.

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:42.448
Those issues

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:43.983
with not really wanting to stop

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.351
are gun reform.

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.452
When we have you know,

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:48.321
we're on the anniversary of the mass

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.622
killing in Buffalo.

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:50.423
That's not the future

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:51.758
most Americans want either.

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:52.592
So

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:54.427
DeSantis isn't X factor in terms

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:55.995
of how he pulls nationally.

00:04:55.995 --> 00:04:57.563
But I don't think the future that he's

00:04:57.563 --> 00:04:58.798
painting is ways

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:00.733
that really play outside of Florida.

00:05:00.733 --> 00:05:01.234
I don't know.

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:02.535
I think that

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:03.436
what DeSantis gives

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:04.637
you is the generational

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:06.873
comparison.

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:07.507
I mean,

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:08.341
you're going to have

00:05:08.341 --> 00:05:10.276
a very old incumbent president

00:05:10.276 --> 00:05:11.978
and a very young up and coming governor.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:12.979
And in some ways,

00:05:12.979 --> 00:05:15.181
I think it pushes the issues aside

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:17.216
and just ask the American people to say,

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:17.483
you know,

00:05:17.483 --> 00:05:18.651
what is the future of our country

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:19.052
look like?

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:20.420
Does it look like someone who will be 86

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.120
at the end of a term,

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:21.354
or does it

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:22.989
look like Ron DeSantis

00:05:22.989 --> 00:05:24.357
and what he's done in Florida?

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:25.425
I don't disagree with you

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:27.327
that some of these policy debates

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:28.661
could make the race interesting,

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:29.495
but I have no doubt

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:30.630
what you said is true.

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.365
Independents do not like Donald Trump.

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:33.066
They've never liked him,

00:05:33.066 --> 00:05:34.767
and he has no plan to win them.

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:35.868
But I could see them

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:37.537
warming up to a younger

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:39.072
Republican candidate

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:40.840
who brings far less drama.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:41.541
I do think, though,

00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:43.543
this is when, like the coalition

00:05:43.543 --> 00:05:44.410
you look at

00:05:44.410 --> 00:05:45.011
when you're thinking about

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:46.212
who can win a race, you're like,

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:48.147
what coalitions can we build?

00:05:48.147 --> 00:05:50.450
I think that maybe independents split

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.552
between Biden and DeSantis,

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:53.720
but young voters really

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:54.954
don't like Ron DeSantis.

00:05:54.954 --> 00:05:56.956
He is come after them.

00:05:56.956 --> 00:05:57.557
I remember like him

00:05:57.557 --> 00:05:58.758
standing behind him,

00:05:58.758 --> 00:06:00.159
young voters overwhelmingly

00:06:00.159 --> 00:06:00.693
despite Joe

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:02.829
Biden's age, showed up in record numbers

00:06:02.829 --> 00:06:03.529
and continue

00:06:03.529 --> 00:06:04.831
to poll really well with him.

00:06:04.831 --> 00:06:06.065
So it will be interesting to see

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:06.833
how it all plays out.

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:08.568
But to Michael's point about the X Factor

00:06:08.568 --> 00:06:09.335
with the Sanders,

00:06:09.335 --> 00:06:10.770
I could see him actually

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:12.538
having the great general election

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:13.773
pivot that we always were like,

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:15.007
this is coming with Donald Trump.

00:06:15.007 --> 00:06:16.676
And of course her does.

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:17.677
I knew him in the House.

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:18.211
He was

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:20.179
pretty much a mainstream Republican

00:06:20.179 --> 00:06:22.081
strong on national defense, somebody who

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:22.982
he will walk back

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.417
that position on Ukraine time

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:25.785
and time over, I think.

00:06:25.785 --> 00:06:26.686
So I could see him

00:06:26.686 --> 00:06:28.321
being somebody who realizes, listen,

00:06:28.321 --> 00:06:29.756
this may be my approach on

00:06:29.756 --> 00:06:31.691
some of these more culture war issues,

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:33.092
but it's not a winning strategy.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:33.559
Let's talk

00:06:33.559 --> 00:06:36.996
about what the president said yesterday

00:06:36.996 --> 00:06:39.065
because he's starting to

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:40.933
put the arguments that he's

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:43.102
making for his reelection

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:44.637
into sharper focus.

00:06:44.637 --> 00:06:46.906
He talked about sinister forces

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:48.808
in America. Let's listen

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:51.444
or those who

00:06:51.444 --> 00:06:52.979
demonize

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:55.581
and pit people against one another.

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:57.183
And there are those

00:06:57.183 --> 00:06:59.619
who do anything and everything

00:06:59.619 --> 00:07:01.788
No matter how desperate or immoral

00:07:01.788 --> 00:07:02.955
to hold on to power.

00:07:02.955 --> 00:07:04.757
But I know this.

00:07:04.824 --> 00:07:06.826
The oldest, most sinister forces

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:08.995
may believe they'll

00:07:08.995 --> 00:07:10.997
determine America's future,

00:07:10.997 --> 00:07:14.434
but they are wrong.

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:16.402
Yeah, I think he was referring to

00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:17.837
the sinister forces out there

00:07:17.837 --> 00:07:19.372
that are embracing right.

00:07:19.372 --> 00:07:20.173
Nationalism

00:07:20.173 --> 00:07:21.774
or the sinister forces out there

00:07:21.774 --> 00:07:24.010
that are rooting for Russia and Putin

00:07:24.377 --> 00:07:26.846
or that are xenophobic.

00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:28.147
And,

00:07:28.214 --> 00:07:31.651
you know, trying to take the rights away

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:32.418
from women

00:07:32.418 --> 00:07:34.654
to do what they can with their bodies.

00:07:34.654 --> 00:07:37.156
And this is particularly

00:07:37.156 --> 00:07:38.357
interesting argument

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:40.393
given you talked about the coalition,

00:07:40.393 --> 00:07:42.028
the fact that enthusiasm

00:07:42.028 --> 00:07:44.030
for President Biden among black

00:07:44.263 --> 00:07:45.598
Democratic voters right

00:07:45.598 --> 00:07:48.000
now, polls show, is pretty low.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:48.301
Yeah.

00:07:48.301 --> 00:07:50.102
And I think what he did was go to them

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:51.571
to have a conversation with them.

00:07:51.571 --> 00:07:53.673
The best thing you can do as a politician

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:54.874
would understand

00:07:54.874 --> 00:07:55.675
is getting criticized

00:07:55.675 --> 00:07:57.076
that he's not talking to human beings.

00:07:57.076 --> 00:07:57.944
Well, Joe Biden says

00:07:57.944 --> 00:07:58.511
I'm going to go

00:07:58.511 --> 00:08:00.012
to a historically black college

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:00.613
and lay out

00:08:00.613 --> 00:08:03.015
why for this new generation of people

00:08:03.015 --> 00:08:03.549
who are voting

00:08:03.549 --> 00:08:05.618
and their parents who go back to all over

00:08:05.618 --> 00:08:07.119
places around the country

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:07.620
and saying

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:10.223
this is why I am running for office.

00:08:10.423 --> 00:08:11.624
This is the real threat.

00:08:11.624 --> 00:08:12.592
